-- title:
--   Frobenius twists act freely on coefficient legs
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ an element, and $r$ a prime number. Let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a nontrivial commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$ of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, subject to two hypotheses: first, every monic polynomial $p \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}[X]$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, in the sense that there is $x \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with $p(x)$ in the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ in $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; second, $\mathrm{Fr}(x) - x^{r}$ lies in that same ideal for every $x \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$. Let $B$ be a nontrivial commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, and let $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism. Write $\mathrm{frobTwist}$ for the twisting operation sending an integer $n$ and such a $\psi$ to the composite $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{n}$. The conclusion is that for integers $a, b$, the equality $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{a} = \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{b}$ of $\mathcal O$-algebra maps forces $a = b$; that is, $\mathbb Z$ acts freely through $\mathrm{frobTwist}$ on the set of $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$.
--
--   This is the freeness statement for the twisted Frobenius action on the unramified coefficients in the Čerednik–Drinfeld setting, where $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ plays the role of the ring of integers of a maximal unramified extension with residue field algebraically closed and $\mathrm{Fr}$ its Frobenius lift. It is used throughout the rigidification bookkeeping for fake elliptic curves, where it pins down the integer exponent attached to a rigidified object from the induced coefficient map alone.
